{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools","id":79003,"title":"Why should Lunars use weapons, armor or other tools?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-24T19:45:00-08:00","id":79003,"title":"Why should Lunars use weapons, armor or other tools?","content":"When you have claws and scales and wings on demand, and the power to assume a thousand forms incapable of holding a bow or sitting astride a horse... why bother with swords, armor or boats?<br /> <br /> Even the hybrid form, which must be human enough to use most forms of tool, is explicitly denied synergy with Artifact Evocations. This reinforces that the Lunar relationship between Fang and Sword is &quot;either/or&quot; without &quot;and&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally speaking, as a group, Lunars are less dependent on external props than anyone else-- from artifacts to infrastructure</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> Yet, the Lunar Exalted will be capable of investing farther into an Artifact's Evocations than Sidereals, despite Sidereals needing to depend much, much more on tools and infrastructure than Lunars. Lunar potential with Evocations is being balanced against the advantages of Deadly Beastman Transformation, such that they are comparably effective and fun.<br /> <br /> But when the major draw of the Lunar Exalted is turning into animals and monsters, what sort of Lunar concepts revolve around tools? What sorts of tools could make that worthwhile?<br /> <br /> Are there ways that the &quot;either/or&quot; relationship of Fang and Sword can be overturned?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T19:57:59-08:00","id":79015,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">That's a lot of questions.<br /> <br /> Q:</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Why should Lunars use weapons, armor or other tools?</span><br /> A: They should use them if what they want to do benefits from using them.<br /> <br /> Q: When you have claws and scales and wings on demand, and the power to assume a thousand forms incapable of holding a bow or sitting astride a horse... why bother with swords, armor or boats?<br /> A: Because that's something you're interested in doing. Yes, a Lunar can live in the woods under the stars, but maybe they'd like to live in a house, sleep in a bed, and eat cooked food off a plate using a fork. Likewise, a Lunar can just run around naked tearing things apart with their teeth and claws, but wearing quicksilver armor that helps protect from the elements and having a bow and arrow to attack at a distance is also nice.<br /> <br /> Q: But when the major draw of the Lunar Exalted is turning into animals and monsters, what sort of Lunar concepts revolve around tools? What sorts of tools could make that worthwhile?<br /> A: Dedicated crafters and tinkerers? Traders and sailors? Healers probably still benefit from medicine. Chefs, novelists... basically any task that isn't 'shit in the woods and kills stuff' will benefit from tool use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T20:13:10-08:00","id":79024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools#post79003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you have claws and scales and wings on demand, and the power to assume a thousand forms incapable of holding a bow or sitting astride a horse... why bother with swords, armor or boats?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know how to answer this without seeming sarcastic. You bother with swords because they're good for killing people without needing to spend motes to grow claws and give away your Anathema status; you wear armor because it's good way to not be stabbed without spending motes; you use boats because they're probably faster than swimming or flying, and they have much less to worry about in terms of being attacked for food or dropping from exhaustion in the middle of of a flight across an ocean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools#post79003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even the hybrid form, which must be human enough to use most forms of tool, is explicitly denied synergy with Artifact Evocations. This reinforces that the Lunar relationship between Fang and Sword is &quot;either/or&quot; without &quot;and.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't heard that, but it sounds like you can still use your sword with your fangs. You just can't use your sword's death beam attack, or whatever evocations actually do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools#post79003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But when the major draw of the Lunar Exalted is turning into animals and monsters, what sort of Lunar concepts revolve around tools?</div> </div> </div> </div>I seem to remember Holden saying something about Lunars being the ones most likely to build an Iron Man suit in a cave with a box of scraps.<br /> <br /> Also, archers and other ranged specialists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools#post79003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What sorts of tools could make that worthwhile?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine a Lunar's approach to tools will be goal-oriented. Like, &quot;Okay, I'm trying to accomplish X, and tools Y and Z will be useful for as long as I need to accomplish X. Once that's done, I won't need Y and Z so much any more.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T20:20:37-08:00","id":79031,"title":"","content":"The one line answer is: Because they are people, and do people things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T22:03:10-08:00","id":79107,"title":"","content":"The best ways to win a fight all involve leveraging advantages, as many as possible, against an opponent. Appropriate equipment is one of the easiest advantages you can acquire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-24T23:11:08-08:00","id":79130,"title":"","content":"Firefox just died on me, so I guess I'm not gonna bother with the sizable post I spent the last 45 minutes on. &gt;_&lt; Trying something shorter...<br /> <br /> Shapeshifting* gives a ton of advantages all by its lonesome (good-to-stellar combat options, amazing stealth/sensory/survival options, unreal mobility options, etc.). Sometimes, yes, these can totally replace tool use -- especially in contexts where &quot;perfect&quot; is way less necessary than &quot;good enough.&quot; When Lunars use tools, they're generally using them for things their shapeshifting can't give them (e.g. using a sword to do battle in when a bestial shape wouldn't get the desired reaction from others; that's aside from particular Evocations**) or in ways that their shapeshifting lets them leverage more effectively (e.g. explosives*** are fucking terrifying in the hands of a Lunar who can (and will) get them places that others can't reasonably check).<br /> <br /> All this is assuming that a Lunar uses shapeshifting at every available opportunity toward the end of some manner of optimization. A Lunar who plainly doesn't want to <i>all</i> the time is perfectly fine, and can get plenty of use from that Swiss army knife in more selective cases. Whether it's a relatively light user like a Lunar swordsman who mainly uses it to get around quickly and prefers to fight as a human or a Lunar fisher who both refuses to give up her family's traditional ways and sees no harm in towing the boat to or from open waters for a catch, or a heavier user like a medicine woman who uses it to help her find and reach the very best ingredients for her craft or an iconoclast who spreads his message and written works by hiding as a beast on the streets as well as selectively taking and using the forms of local officials, shapeshifting remains enormously valuable to every Lunar.<br /> <br /> ugh i'm sleepy and that last bit felt like empty vague and pointless generalizing bah<br /> <br /> * I'm still not clear enough on all that their Charmset can give them, so I'll mostly leave it out of this. Just presume it proves generally helpful in almost all situations, though definitely some more than others and it may sometimes demand a more oblique/indirect/creative application.<br /> <br /> ** I can see no small number of Lunars who don't see the point of using Evocations for combat and combat alone: they've always got DBT right there. As a result, such Lunars favor Evocations in their weapons and other Artifacts that do other things, or have special traits they find helpful for more than raw combat enhancement.<br /> <br /> *** I can't remember at this moment how rare and dangerous explosives or functional explosives are meant to be in the setting. This does little to change how an individual with shapeshifting has a lot of power to leverage with them.<br /> <br /> Just as a potential point of reference, here are Holden's quotes on a relevant topic, the one JimB was getting at (located <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Exalts#Lunars\" target=\"_blank\">hereabouts on the Wiki</a>):<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shapeshifting doesn't help you with [making daiklaves or repairing the weather controls in Rathess or the like]. (Well, I mean, maybe you could turn into a mouse to crawl inside a sky mantis tower and jigger some delicate parts back into alignment by hand? I dunno. Mostly it doesn't.)<br /> <br /> It's not like Lunars have some kind of special brain damage that makes them less-able to learn things than other Exalts. They can study Lore, Craft, Occult, sure. Their magic isn't the best in the world at building stuff, although they have stuff to help with it. They're certainly not the peers of the Solars in that category or anything (but then, who is?).<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, as a group, Lunars are less dependent on external props than anyone else-- from artifacts to infrastructure-- and this is one reason why they tend to favor simple, robust tools that are either very difficult to break, or which are easy to replace.<br /> <br /> That said, keep in mind-- they have Intelligence Charms. You will, from time to time, see Lunar Tony Stark building amazing shit in a cave, out of scraps. But as a whole they don't trend toward sophisticated big-scale manufacturing projects, in large part because the majority of Lunars don't like doing anything that requires them to set up an immobile and semi-permanent base of operations, like a fully-stocked-and-kitted artificer's workshop. It's more common to see a Lunar set up a temporary work site, build a daiklave or some armor or some similar piece of personal kit for himself or for someone else, and then break down the site, hide any of the components he can't easily replace, and then move on until he needs it again some years later. Most Lunars operate on wartime footing at all times, and they are all priority targets.*<br /> <br /> *There are exceptions to all these things, and they tend to be interesting subjects in their own right.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mmm. Just keep in mind that I said &quot;amazing shit&quot; rather than &quot;power armor&quot; or &quot;warstriders&quot; intentionally. When you go off the grid, you don't get the benefits of the grid, so to speak. That still leaves the ability to make moonsilver plate, personal weapons, mystic veils, and other such magical wonders well within your capabilities-- and frankly, those things are generally better-suited to Lunar endeavors than something that needs specialist personnel to maintain and repair and a manse to keep it running anyway.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for someone that can outperform a maxed out Solar artifact-crafter-- you're not going to find one. If you're looking to play a Lunar that can make cool artifacts and enhance the story, sure. 3e crafting should be fun, whichever kind of Exalt you're playing.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T09:49:47-08:00","id":79402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=79024#post79024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't heard that, but it sounds like you can still use your sword with your fangs. You just can't use your sword's death beam attack, or whatever evocations actually do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember that. It was mentioned as a possible way to have a character who doesn't use DBT in battle without feeling like an idiot because DBT has all advantages no disadvantages.<br /> <br /> It was a while ago, so it's possible the devs have changed their minds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T10:10:26-08:00","id":79416,"title":"","content":"There's the possibility that the lunar is posing as something else too, and in doing so, he can't transform without blowing his cover. I once used a lunar as a knight in a kingdom. He was posing as a god-blood for... reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1g_IC644YJoiVAm6ngqcBmsQtff2YYtd3pDbZpaOxx4o\" target=\"_blank\">My Exalted Character Creation Tool may be downloaded here.</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1086797-demac-s-exalted-character-creation-tool\" target=\"_blank\">The thread talking about the tool can be found here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1136654-exalted-seats-of-power\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted: Seats of Power is a homebrewed manse creation system.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1oaq3wk7lJKZ022SUA4iPfGzMpmBTNXlM\" target=\"_blank\">I have a rewrite of the craft system which can be downloaded here.</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1070312-i-got-my-book-it-s-super-fancy-and-i-can-t-read-the-cover/page2\" target=\"_blank\">I like the Mesoamerican look</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2346-demac","name":"Demac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T10:38:46-08:00","id":79435,"title":"","content":"If a master swordsman is chosen as a Lunar, she isn't going to just throw away those twenty years of experience to go flail about with gigantic animal limbs. She's going to be a master Lunar swordsman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T11:15:55-08:00","id":79456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=79435#post79435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a master swordsman is chosen as a Lunar, she isn't going to just throw away those twenty years of experience to go flail about with gigantic animal limbs. She's going to be a master Lunar swordsman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you turn into <a href=\"http://www.toyark.com/attachments/1097d1235367769-ptru1-5444765dt.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this guy</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T12:28:35-08:00","id":79501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=79435#post79435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a master swordsman is chosen as a Lunar, she isn't going to just throw away those twenty years of experience to go flail about with gigantic animal limbs. She's going to be a master Lunar swordsman.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or you turn into a sword and let the nearby Solar flail about with you... while commenting on his terrible technique. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T12:58:13-08:00","id":79532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools#post79003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you have claws and scales and wings on demand, and the power to assume a thousand forms incapable of holding a bow or sitting astride a horse... why bother with swords, armor or boats?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because swords, armor and boats:<br /> <br /> * Are often more powerful (in terms of damage, accuracy, or any other measurable stat) than anything you can get from beast forms, especially if they're artifacts. If they weren't, mortals would just be using claws and scales harvested off animals they've killed. (Note that where swords are unavailable, or the local animals have really really good claws, mortals do just that.)<br /> <br /> * Typically don't cost motes for each use (or at least to deploy them for use), unlike most of a Lunar's powers.<br /> <br /> * Can be made of moonsilver (at least the swords and armor), which make them work even when in those thousand forms.<br /> <br /> Use the shapeshifting to do what your tools can not, not as an excuse to shun readily available tools.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/240-winged-cat","name":"Winged Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar240_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T12:59:44-08:00","id":79536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=79435#post79435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a master swordsman is chosen as a Lunar, she isn't going to just throw away those twenty years of experience to go flail about with gigantic animal limbs. She's going to be a master Lunar swordsman.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll admit, I wasn't thinking of that angle.<br /> <br /> Still, the master swordsman who becomes a Lunar can fight with swords in hybrid form (and Morke seemed to imply that starting with DBT is automatic now). The Lunar swordsman would definitely have an incentive to acquire an artifact replacement for his original sword, but what's his incentive to develop Evocations that he cannot use because of Deadly Beastman Transformation?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T13:06:01-08:00","id":79543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=79536#post79536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit, I wasn't thinking of that angle.<br /> <br /> Still, the master swordsman who becomes a Lunar can fight with swords in hybrid form (and Morke seemed to imply that starting with DBT is automatic now). The Lunar swordsman would definitely have an incentive to acquire an artifact replacement for his original sword, but what's his incentive to develop Evocations that he cannot use because of Deadly Beastman Transformation?</div> </div> </div> </div>I shall repeat my prior thought:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=79130#post79130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see no small number of Lunars who don't see the point of using Evocations for combat and combat alone: they've always got DBT right there. As a result, such Lunars favor Evocations in their weapons and other Artifacts that do other things, or have special traits they find helpful for more than raw combat enhancement.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T13:29:36-08:00","id":79579,"title":"","content":"The Lunar has a house, armor, swords, and boats, because they are useful. But when you come in and burn down his house, and his boats, and secure his swords and armor so he doesn't have access to them, that Lunar takes you apart with his bare hands. Or maybe he puts together a quick rudimentary spear that is robust, efficient, and deadly. Or slap some obsidian chunks into a piece of wood and rip someone's head off with it. Lunars use tools because tools are good. When a Lunar doesn't have those tools, he uses what he still has at hand. Or, he uses his hands.<br /> <br /> This is at least the way I've always looked at Lunars. Love tools for what they can do, but never, ever rely on them, because someone can take them away. Or they can break. Or maybe you just couldn't carry all the tools you need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2132-ejtaka","name":"Ejtaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2132_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1064"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T14:04:32-08:00","id":79618,"title":"","content":"Do you need to sprout fur and fangs to fight like a monster?<br /> <br /> A Wyld Hunt sent to kill a pair of Lunars will be wary of the savage wolf-beast that lurks in the shadows, with fangs that can pierce chain mail and jaws that can break iron bars. They will also be wary of the muttering man with the shuffling step, eyes glimmering as he bites at his shield and twirls his axe, just <i>daring</i> them to attack him.<br /> <br /> Presumably in 3rd edition, Lunars who choose Evocations over DBT will still have considerable native combat tech to back said Evocations up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","user":"GhostTurtle","date":". 02-25-2014, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1180-ghostturtle","name":"GhostTurtle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T16:33:20-08:00","id":79741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=79130#post79130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see no small number of Lunars who don't see the point of using Evocations for combat and combat alone: they've always got DBT right there. As a result, such Lunars favor Evocations in their weapons and other Artifacts that do other things, or have special traits they find helpful for more than raw combat enhancement.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Sword of Omens, give me Sight Beyond Sight!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, I started this thread late at night, and so missed my focus a little.<br /> <br /> I wasn't so much curious about why a Lunar would use any tools at all, but why he would max out his Evocations with an artifact, or go to any trouble to get special tools like artifact boats or godblooded horses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 02-25-2014, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-25T16:51:50-08:00","id":79760,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna say this: some species of Gorilla (simplification) use sticks and stone as very crude tools. Have you seen the jaws of a gorilla? Have you seen the muscles on their arms? These creatures can rip a man into shreds. They still use tools.<br /> <br /> You know why? Because tools are more useful for some things then their big clumsy arms that evolved to grab and punch things. And gorillas are smart enough to know that. Would you say that your avarage Lunar is dumber than a gorilla?<br /> <br /> That's a hell of a statement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2052-frombeyond","name":"FromBeyond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"426"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T19:41:56-08:00","id":80725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=79741#post79741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Sword of Omens, give me Sight Beyond Sight!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Incidentally, I started this thread late at night, and so missed my focus a little.<br /> <br /> I wasn't so much curious about why a Lunar would use any tools at all, but why he would max out his Evocations with an artifact, or go to any trouble to get special tools like artifact boats or godblooded horses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so what you're getting at is &quot;Given the substantial opportunity cost of getting <i>mechanically-useful</i> tools instead of more intrinsic power, and that tools can be lost, broken, or taken away while intrinsic powers can't, why would a Lunar invest in the former and not the latter?&quot; In 2E and 2.5E, the answers would be:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Maintaining a cover ID</li> <li>Doing something intrinsic powers don't cover, or</li> <li>Aesthetics</li> </ol>1 and 2 are things that, in theory, can be fun and interesting but, the way the rules handled it in prior editions, were generally not. 3 is something I don't really care to have players pay for. Depending on how pervasive the system conceit of 'Low buy-in to competence, high buy-in to mastery' is, I'm hoping 3E will add to that list:<br /> <br /> 4. Because branching out is now just as valid a choice as hyper-specializing, and the game engine will no longer go out of its way to punish you for Spending XP Wrong, and<br /> 5. There are distinct strengths and weaknesses to both shapeshifting and external tools, such that you could justify a focus (or lack thereof) on either<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-26T21:19:54-08:00","id":80788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=79741#post79741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't so much curious about why a Lunar would use any tools at all, but why he would max out his Evocations with an artifact, or go to any trouble to get special tools like artifact boats or godblooded horses.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda feel like a lot of the examples and reasons for the one will be true of the other. Lunars could still gladly master all the Evocations on an artifact weapon even with a mutually exclusive DBT as an option. The situation probably analogues to a Solar maxing out the Evocations on multiple mutually exclusive artifact weapons. Evocations don't sound like they're meant to be pushover effects:* having multiple awesome options that wouldn't otherwise be available is reason enough.<br /> <br /> Besides, from a more gamist perspective, all Exalts will have regular XP as well as Solar XP,** the latter of which can be spent on basically anything <i>except</i> native Charms. Without competition from Charms, Evocations might look a sight more attractive to a Lunar for that Solar XP. The competition for Solar XP is thus mostly between the relatively boring -- but serviceable and reliable -- Ability/Attribute advancement, and the flashier and potent -- albeit perhaps situational -- trio of Evocations, Martial Arts, and Sorcery.*** It doesn't feel like a given choice need be better than any other.<br /> <br /> * Remember, we've only got one real example so far: Stormcaller initiates a hurricane when drawn. Holden talked about it with us at Aggiecon, and gave the impression that's not just a visual effect. Even if they can't get up to the apex Evocation's massive stormblast, Lunars keen on breaking the Realm's shit would eat that up.<br /> <br /> ** Would still go for a different name, but whatevs.<br /> <br /> *** Evocations as situational things with DBT right there goes without saying. Each Martial Arts style**** has a kind of paper-rock-scissors-ish relationship with other styles/obstacles, so a given style won't always be a good idea. We don't know the new build of Sorcery, but the last word ages ago spoke of special actions and tools to gather motes for a spell; whatever the case, powerful though it may be, it doesn't sound like Sorcery is always easy or convenient to use.<br /> <br /> **** Have I mentioned my interest in a Lunar Martial Artist who switches from style to style as well as from shape to shape in combat? Because that interest exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T13:51:09-08:00","id":81214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=79741#post79741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't so much curious about why a Lunar would use any tools at all, but why he would max out his Evocations with an artifact, or go to any trouble to get special tools like artifact boats or godblooded horses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the Lunar wants to reap the considerable benefits of having maxed-out Evocations on top of his natural puissance. Or to have a boat that is better than mundane boats, for purposes of transporting people other than himself across the sea quicker and more comfortably than he could by going orca-form and letting them ride in his mouth. Or because he is a legendary horseman, and seeks a steed worth of him in its saddle. Those are all pretty natural ambitions, if you're an Exalt who wants to gain power, and there's no compelling reason not for them to apply to Lunars. Now, a Lunar <i>could</i> shun the legendary sword and instead dedicate himself to perfecting his body as a living weapon, or just take some aquatic forms and not worry about having a crew/cargo, or just turn into a horse himself. But just because they can pick option B doesn't mean they should be disallowed or disincentivized from taking option A.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T16:44:51-08:00","id":81314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GhostTurtle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=79618#post79618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Wyld Hunt sent to kill a pair of Lunars will be wary of the savage wolf-beast that lurks in the shadows, with fangs that can pierce chain mail and jaws that can break iron bars. They will also be wary of the muttering man with the shuffling step, eyes glimmering as he bites at his shield and twirls his axe, just <i>daring</i> them to attack him.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they will <i>completely miss</i> the charming little socialite mayor of the town (who just happens to eat people - body and souls - in their sleep, leaving no evidence) and her alchemist friend/lover/whatever-they're-calling-themselves-this-week (who merges with the earth, walls, or any solid surface, drags enemies into himself, and smothers/crushes them, thus ritually &quot;burying&quot; his victims to prevent ghosts from rising), if they ignore anyone using non-combat tools and trappings of civilization as &quot;obviously not a Lunar, because why would a Lunar care?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/240-winged-cat","name":"Winged Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar240_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-27T18:11:04-08:00","id":81346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=81214#post81214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But just because they can pick option B doesn't mean they should be disallowed or disincentivized from taking option A.</div> </div> </div> </div>My curiosity is more &quot;are these options incentivized <i>enough </i>for players to care.&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, no. Obviously, you guys are doing your best on that front. So my curiosity is &quot;<i>how </i>will these options be incentivized enough&quot;, and I created this topic (however poorly) with the intent of brainstorming together with the forum on such methods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T15:41:10-08:00","id":83537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=81346#post81346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My curiosity is more &quot;are these options incentivized <i>enough </i>for players to care.&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, no. Obviously, you guys are doing your best on that front. So my curiosity is &quot;<i>how </i>will these options be incentivized enough&quot;, and I created this topic (however poorly) with the intent of brainstorming together with the forum on such methods.</div> </div> </div> </div>My question would be:<br /> <br /> If tools are so f***ing bloody awesome, then why would a Lunar ever want to use shapeshifting? If Evocations are so useful I'm going to want to pursue them even if I can't use them with DBT, then why would I want to learn DBT and lock myself out of all the XP (or other character resource) I spent learning those amazing Evocations? If the party's artifact airship can fly faster than my Mospid form, then what use is it? If Moonsilver Armour is going to protect me more than Elephant Hide, then why shouldn't I spend my Merit points on Artifact instead of Heart's Blood?<br /> <br /> Of course the person who invests in both tools and native powers is going to be more flexible, able to use tools where she can and falling back on her body when she can't. But will the structure of the game support this flexibility? Because every iteration of Exalted so far (and WW games in general... and RPGs in general) has gone the opposite route and has incentivised specialisation over generalism - the character with Martial Arts 0, Melee 4, Dex 5, Strength 1, is always going to beat the character with Martial Arts 2, Melee 2, Dex 3, Strength 2. If the rules are unbalanced, you can pass the buck to the ST, but it's still going to boil down to the permissive ST (under which tools will always be better because he won't take them away) or the evil ST (under whom native powers will always be better because he'll steal your tools at every opportunity).<br /> <br /> tl;dr<br /> <br /> If Lunars are supposed to use tools and their own powers, how will this be balanced?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T16:51:26-08:00","id":83590,"title":"","content":"Unlike Solars, who can create toilet paper using Glorious Solar Tissues, Lunars tend to not use toilet paper, and instead have a Strength charm to let them clench their buttcheeks so hard that it turns poop into diamonds.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I considered about posting this when the thread first came up and thought better of it, but if it's going to be on the front page for a week, well <i>fine </i>then","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T17:39:06-08:00","id":83629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=83537#post83537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Lunars are supposed to use tools and their own powers, how will this be balanced?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you equally concerned about Artifacts overpowering Solar Charms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T17:42:02-08:00","id":83632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=83537#post83537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Lunars are supposed to use tools and their own powers, how will this be balanced?</div> </div> </div> </div>How is a Solar supposed to use his barehands and a bow?<br /> <br /> &quot;Supposed to&quot; is the wrong phrase. A Solar can choose to specialize in Brawl or Melee; he is not forced to take either, much less to generalize with both. Likewise, a Lunar can choose to specialize in the Martial Arts Ability and combat animal forms, or he can choose to specialize in the Melee Ability, acquire an artifact weapon, and invest in Evocations; he can also choose both or neither.<br /> <br /> Can the Solar fight with a sword in one hand and the other hand empty? Yes, and Lunars will more than likely have the option of switching forms between one attack and another, so that they can stomp someone as an elephant and then stab the broken heap with a spear.<br /> <br /> Remember that Holden and John were experimenting with a new Protean keyword in Exalted 2.5, which would allow a Lunar to reflexively assume a form appropriate to that Charm. So a Lunar could freely shapeshift into various combat-appropriate beasts just by using his combat Charms like he always would. If the Protean keyword doesn't return in Third Edition, it will be because they found a more elegant solution.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the character with Martial Arts 0, Melee 4, Dex 5, Strength 1, is always going to beat the character with Martial Arts 2, Melee 2, Dex 3, Strength 2 </div> </div> </div>That might matter in Burn Legend story-free tournaments, but not so much in Exalted.<br /> <br /> &quot;Player versus player&quot; combat is the central thesis of Burn Legend, but Exalted is about telling a story which often happens to involve combat, usually between players and non-player characters, and where &quot;beating the other guy soundly&quot; is not always the necessary win condition.<br /> <br /> In Exalted, generalization should be rewarded with additional scenes in which the character can contribute, because Exalted is a storytelling game.<br /> <br /> If a generalist PC is losing a fight to a special NPC, that's not the fault of the system. That's either the Storyteller's fault for not understanding (or caring) about a proper difficult threshold, or your fault for trying to fight an opponent on his own terms when you should be trying to assert your own terms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=83590#post83590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unlike Solars, who can create toilet paper using Glorious Solar Tissues, Lunars tend to not use toilet paper, and instead have a Strength charm to let them clench their buttcheeks so hard that it turns poop into diamonds.<br /> <br /> \u200bI considered about posting this when the thread first came up and thought better of it, but if it's going to be on the front page for a week, well <i>fine </i>then</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you waited, because I wouldn't have appreciated your post like I do today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T19:06:39-08:00","id":83667,"title":"","content":"Fighting style is a qualitative choice. Trying to quantify it - or building a combat engine designed to quantify it - creates problems. <br /> <br /> Which is why I'm really excited about standardized weapon stats that emphasize tags over damage and accuracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T20:09:45-08:00","id":83714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=83590#post83590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unlike Solars, who can create toilet paper using Glorious Solar Tissues, Lunars tend to not use toilet paper, and instead have a Strength charm to let them clench their buttcheeks so hard that it turns poop into diamonds.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Here you go - one dragon diamond, freshly minted from Quark's keester.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T20:45:21-08:00","id":83735,"title":"","content":"Stabbing someone with a sword tends to draw slightly less attention then turning into a giant god monster and tearing their head off, some people don't like drawing attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T21:20:21-08:00","id":83744,"title":"","content":"I always felt that if there was one type of Exalt that could completely forego tools and equipment in favor of their own inherent abilities, it would be the Lunars.<br /> <br /> That said, while it would be cool for it to be an option for them, I don't think they should be shoehorned in to being &quot;the equipmentless exalt&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-03T23:13:53-08:00","id":83799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=83537#post83537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question would be:<br /> <br /> If tools are so f***ing bloody awesome, then why would a Lunar ever want to use shapeshifting? If Evocations are so useful I'm going to want to pursue them even if I can't use them with DBT, then why would I want to learn DBT and lock myself out of all the XP (or other character resource) I spent learning those amazing Evocations? If the party's artifact airship can fly faster than my Mospid form, then what use is it? If Moonsilver Armour is going to protect me more than Elephant Hide, then why shouldn't I spend my Merit points on Artifact instead of Heart's Blood?<br /> <br /> tl;dr<br /> <br /> If Lunars are supposed to use tools and their own powers, how will this be balanced?</div> </div> </div> </div>If eyes are so fucking bloody awesome, then why would a human being ever use his hands?<br /> <br /> Shapeshifting is rad. It is shifting forms mid-combat to use the hunting styles of different animals tactically and spying on your enemies for miles on the wings of an eagle and turning into a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Entelodont\" target=\"_blank\">hellboar</a> to dispose of a corpse by eating it. Evocations (and artifacts in general) are also rad. The places where their effects are 100% redundant are very, very few. The relationship between them isn't one of stronger or weaker, but just two tools you can use to build your character. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T10:00:20-08:00","id":84024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=83799#post83799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If eyes are so fucking bloody awesome, then why would a human being ever use his hands?<br /> <br /> Shapeshifting is rad. It is shifting forms mid-combat to use the hunting styles of different animals tactically and spying on your enemies for miles on the wings of an eagle and turning into a <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Entelodont\" target=\"_blank\">hellboar</a> to dispose of a corpse by eating it. Evocations (and artifacts in general) are also rad. The places where their effects are 100% redundant are very, very few. The relationship between them isn't one of stronger or weaker, but just two tools you can use to build your character.</div> </div> </div> </div>So there won't have an artifact that lets them spy on their enemies for miles? You won't be able to summon a hellboar to eat corpses? Will I be able to use Evocations and Protean shapeshifting mid-combat - or will the action economy force me to take one or the other?<br /> <br /> E2.5 gives me the choice of spending 5BPs on taking a flying horse as a Familiar, 1BP on taking an Agata as a Demonic Familiar or 8BP on learning Demon of the First Circle. They are all &quot;tools I can use to build my character&quot; but one of these options is clearly &quot;stronger&quot; than the &quot;weaker&quot; ones.<br /> <br /> I'm not having a go at you. E3 seems to be really well designed (from what has been revealed so far), and if you don't think that redundancy exists been shapeshifting and artifacts,then I'm going to give my thumbs up and eagerly await the book. I like your work. I trust you know what you're doing. The OP was asking &quot;are artifacts going to be underpowered&quot;, I am asking &quot;are artifacts going to be overpowered&quot;. If you're going to sit there and tell me &quot;no&quot;, then that's my question answered. Can't wait to build a character that I want to build rather than the character that the rules system shoehorns me into.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=83629#post83629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you equally concerned about Artifacts overpowering Solar Charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, actually. And vice-versa.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to play a Solar swordsman in 2nd, then you needed to have an Artifact sword (otherwise you'd be spending too many motes to attack and breaking your sword every time you got attacked). I would love to be able to play a Solar swordsman in 3rd who didn't <i>have</i> to start play with a diaklave so I could play though the interesting story of finding a diaklave in a tomb (or looting it from the Wyld Hunt).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=83632#post83632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is a Solar supposed to use his barehands and a bow?</div> </div> </div> </div>Learn Wood Dragon Style. You get synergy between your ranged attacks and your barehanded attacks. You don't get things like &quot;you can't use Evocations if you've taken your Deadly Beastman Transformation.... because we the developers don't like how cool Deadly Beastman Transformation is&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=83632#post83632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Supposed to&quot; is the wrong phrase. A Solar can choose to specialize in Brawl or Melee; he is not forced to take either, much less to generalize with both. Likewise, a Lunar can choose to specialize in the Martial Arts Ability and combat animal forms, or he can choose to specialize in the Melee Ability, acquire an artifact weapon, and invest in Evocations; he can also choose both or neither.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then your answer to &quot;Why should Lunars use weapons, armour or other tools?&quot; is &quot;they can if they want to and they shouldn't if they don't want to&quot;?<br /> <br /> Which is actually a really good answer that gets me hyped for 3rd. But it's an answer that's somewhat different from the prevailing opinion in this thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=83632#post83632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can the Solar fight with a sword in one hand and the other hand empty? Yes, and Lunars will more than likely have the option of switching forms between one attack and another, so that they can stomp someone as an elephant and then stab the broken heap with a spear.<br /> <br /> Remember that Holden and John were experimenting with a new Protean keyword in Exalted 2.5, which would allow a Lunar to reflexively assume a form appropriate to that Charm. So a Lunar could freely shapeshift into various combat-appropriate beasts just by using his combat Charms like he always would. If the Protean keyword doesn't return in Third Edition, it will be because they found a more elegant solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds cool. And Vance's comment also seems to back this up. Thanks for the helpful reply.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=83632#post83632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Combat balance] might matter in Burn Legend story-free tournaments, but not so much in Exalted.<br /> <br /> &quot;Player versus player&quot; combat is the central thesis of Burn Legend, but Exalted is about telling a story which often happens to involve combat, usually between players and non-player characters, and where &quot;beating the other guy soundly&quot; is not always the necessary win condition.<br /> <br /> In Exalted, generalization should be rewarded with additional scenes in which the character can contribute, because Exalted is a storytelling game.<br /> <br /> If a generalist PC is losing a fight to a special NPC, that's not the fault of the system. That's either the Storyteller's fault for not understanding (or caring) about a proper difficult threshold, or your fault for trying to fight an opponent on his own terms when you should be trying to assert your own terms</div> </div> </div> </div>E2 made balancing a combat encounter as an ST very difficult, as a foe that could easily kill 80% of the Circle could be curb-stomped in 3 ticks by the other 20%. So speaking as an ST... combat balance <i>does</i> matter. E2 especially (and E1 also) pushed a &quot;you should be a generalist&quot; agenda in fluff, but every mechanic published promoted specialisation and synergistic mechanics that would make a generalist viable (like the Protean keyword) were few and far between. If that is going to chance and the game will support having eyes and hands working together then that is FANTASTIC. It answers my question perfectly and puts all my fears as an ST to rest.<br /> <br /> Speaking with my &quot;player&quot; hat on: combat also tends to be the most dramatic and <i>fun</i> part of a game, I don't have a lot of fun when my character is vastly over-shone in their supposed area of expertise by another party member. Being able to participate in combat, but lose AND being able to participate in a seduction, but get a drink thrown in my face AND being able to participate in studying the Broken Winged Crane, but getting sucked into Malfeas might be fun the first few times, but constantly sucking at everything (as a generalist) gets old really quickly. Far more fun to specialise and feel the triumph of winning that combat (before getting a drink thrown in my face and being cast into Maffeas).<br /> <br /> If everyone plays a generalist, then that's not a problem. The game mechanics might reward specialisation, but if all the players take an equal handicap then the ST can compensate. But most groups I've played with don't railroad players into hamstringing their characters except as a last resort. I don't want to play someone who sucks. And I don't want to play a pregenerated character. I want to create a character that I think is interesting and I want to be one of the heroes of the story. I want to &quot;win&quot;. I don't mind ending up like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BqrkWLXK7wQ\" target=\"_blank\">Rameriez</a> but I don't want to end up like <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FiN6NDmONFM\" target=\"_blank\">Reek</a>..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 03-04-2014, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T10:19:12-08:00","id":84037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=83735#post83735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stabbing someone with a sword tends to draw slightly less attention then turning into a giant god monster and tearing their head off, some people don't like drawing attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using a moonsilver daiklave's Evocation will probably be very attention-grabbing. Even simply stabbing someone with a moonsilver daiklave would be attention-grabbing. Hell, <i>owning</i> a moonsilver daiklave would be attention-grabbing, such that being furry only confirms people's suspicions.<br /> <br /> But perhaps you came in only after I clarified my intent, but didn't read that far before posting. Or before finding the half-dozen other posts which already said what you did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T10:37:48-08:00","id":84047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84024#post84024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there won't have an artifact that lets them spy on their enemies for miles? You won't be able to summon a hellboar to eat corpses? Will I be able to use Evocations and Protean shapeshifting mid-combat - or will the action economy force me to take one or the other?</div> </div> </div> </div>These are not invalid questions to ask, but you won't get the response you want from Robert because your tone is belligerent. Even when you're upset, you shouldn't phrase your questions like you want to pick a fight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> E2.5 gives me the choice of spending 5BPs on taking a flying horse as a Familiar, 1BP on taking an Agata as a Demonic Familiar or 8BP on learning Demon of the First Circle. They are all &quot;tools I can use to build my character&quot; but one of these options is clearly &quot;stronger&quot; than the &quot;weaker&quot; ones. </div> </div> </div>I honestly don't know -- can demonic familiars be sorcerously banished like normal? Because that would make the non-demon pegasus more advantageous in particular situations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The OP was asking &quot;are artifacts going to be underpowered&quot; </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's what I said? Certainly that's nothing close to what I meant to ask.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't get things like &quot;you can't use Evocations if you've taken your Deadly Beastman Transformation.... because we the developers don't like how cool Deadly Beastman Transformation is&quot;. </div> </div> </div>It's best not to look at this as nerfing Lunar Evocations or Warforms, but as making both options so powerful that, if Lunars could use both of them together at once, the Solar Exalted wouldn't have the greatest potential as warriors.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then your answer to &quot;Why should Lunars use weapons, armour or other tools?&quot; is &quot;they can if they want to and they shouldn't if they don't want to&quot;?<br /> <br /> Which is actually a really good answer that gets me hyped for 3rd. But it's an answer that's somewhat different from the prevailing opinion in this thread. </div> </div> </div><b>My actual question was something very different, but I lost it when writing the original post and it came out all wrong.<br /> <br /> If I have any question remaining, it's something like, &quot;Why are Lunars better at Evocations than Sidereals despite a greater incentive to forego tools altogether?&quot;</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T10:54:45-08:00","id":84062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84037#post84037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using a moonsilver daiklave's Evocation will probably be very attention-grabbing. Even simply stabbing someone with a moonsilver daiklave would be attention-grabbing. Hell, <i>owning</i> a moonsilver daiklave would be attention-grabbing, such that being furry only confirms people's suspicions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Y'know, even if full-blown Lunar Blade Reconfiguration-style weapon-morphing is out, I could totally get behind moonsilver artifacts being able to 'consume' other items like a Lunar does with HB shapes, giving options for mutating between fixed 'presets', including mundane forms or similar options that facilitate disguise or blending in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T10:55:55-08:00","id":84064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84047#post84047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>My actual question was something very different, but I lost it when writing the original post and it came out all wrong.<br /> <br /> If I have any question remaining, it's something like, &quot;Why are Lunars better at Evocations than Sidereals despite a greater incentive to forego tools altogether?&quot;</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting question. It's probably because Lunars have a wider range of tools (in a broad sense of the words) available to them, whereas Sidereals are designed to work with a much more limited range of tools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T11:01:31-08:00","id":84066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84064#post84064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting question. It's probably because Lunars have a wider range of tools (in a broad sense of the words) available to them, whereas Sidereals are designed to work with a much more limited range of tools.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sids might also just not disengage from Evocations when using SMA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T11:05:14-08:00","id":84070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84024#post84024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking with my &quot;player&quot; hat on: combat also tends to be the most dramatic and <i>fun</i> part of a game, I don't have a lot of fun when my character is vastly over-shone in their supposed area of expertise by another party member. Being able to participate in combat, but lose AND being able to participate in a seduction, but get a drink thrown in my face AND being able to participate in studying the Broken Winged Crane, but getting sucked into Malfeas might be fun the first few times, but constantly sucking at everything (as a generalist) gets old really quickly. Far more fun to specialise and feel the triumph of winning that combat (before getting a drink thrown in my face and being cast into Maffeas).</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that this problem was pretty much directly caused by 2e being set up in such a way that a relatively high degree of specialization was required to meaningfully participate in any particular activity.<br /> <br /> Compare, say, D&amp;D, where, say, a bard can participate in level-appropriate combat encounters without either outshining the combat specialist or getting splattered in two hits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T11:16:18-08:00","id":84073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84037#post84037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using a moonsilver daiklave's Evocation will probably be very attention-grabbing. Even simply stabbing someone with a moonsilver daiklave would be attention-grabbing. Hell, <i>owning</i> a moonsilver daiklave would be attention-grabbing, such that being furry only confirms people's suspicions.<br /> <br /> But perhaps you came in only after I clarified my intent, but didn't read that far before posting. Or before finding the half-dozen other posts which already said what you did.</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer is more interesting, it was five in the morning and I was baked on sleeping pills (trying to stay awake after taking zolpidem results in mind altering effects).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T11:46:29-08:00","id":84085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84024#post84024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can't wait to build a character that I want to build rather than the character that the rules system shoehorns me into.<br /> [...]<br /> You don't get things like &quot;you can't use Evocations if you've taken your Deadly Beastman Transformation.... because we the developers don't like how cool Deadly Beastman Transformation is&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, wait, you don't want Solars to be forced to take an artifact weapon at chargen because you can't use your perfect parry effectively without one, but you're OK with Lunars being forced to take DBT because it has no downside whatsoever?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T11:56:56-08:00","id":84092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84070#post84070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that this problem was pretty much directly caused by 2e being set up in such a way that a relatively high degree of specialization was required to meaningfully participate in any particular activity.<br /> <br /> Compare, say, D&amp;D, where, say, a bard can participate in level-appropriate combat encounters without either outshining the combat specialist or getting splattered in two hits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hopefully with what we've seen from third edition the next edition will be like this. I actually played a bard in a couple of games of DnD and I can say from personal experience that it's definitely fun to do a bit of everything. You get to be a wizard who draws his rapier and flourishes it menacingly, and you get to tell everyone the ancient lore of the world while being the faceman frontline fighter. Anything you can do someone else can do better, but you can do anything you please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T12:41:36-08:00","id":84137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84064#post84064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting question. It's probably because Lunars have a wider range of tools (in a broad sense of the words) available to them, whereas Sidereals are designed to work with a much more limited range of tools.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may also be that a Lunar is geared more toward being overtly powerful in a personal sense and flexible in a situation, whereas a Sidereal shows greater power in an indirect fashion and after getting everything into place. &quot;Sidereals get everything into place before they can show their true power,&quot; actually sounds like it's reflected in their mastery of the martial arts, from Vance's description: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/74101-3e-questions-on-twitter-with-mr-vance?p=75339#post75339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crane vs Single Point Shining Into The Void is the most ridiculous shit, because each style is doing exactly what the other style wants its enemy to be doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T18:34:06-08:00","id":84321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84047#post84047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I have any question remaining, it's something like, &quot;Why are Lunars better at Evocations than Sidereals despite a greater incentive to forego tools altogether?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's less a statement of how good Lunars are at Evocations, and more one of how restricted Sidereals when it comes to accessing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T19:37:09-08:00","id":84336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84321#post84321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's less a statement of how good Lunars are at Evocations, and more one of how restricted Sidereals when it comes to accessing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I wish to access the Terrible Radiance Beam!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You're not cleared for that. ACCESS DENIED.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-04T23:45:07-08:00","id":84436,"title":"","content":"What about the animals that lack fang &amp; claw?<br /> <br /> My favorite Lunar was nicknamed 'Punchy T. Hoss'. He was a horse who... punched stuff. He used brawling aids (God-Kicking boots and Smashfists that became his horseshoes, naturally) to great effect. Sure, he could use a sword, and did from time to time, but it was not his thing.<br /> <br /> Not all Lunars have predatory totems, and not every lunar invests deeply into the charms allowing them to add features to their DBT form. Splish-Splash the Koi Lunar likely uses whatever weapon she can get her fins on. Lady Prances the Reindeer lunar doesn't like guts in her horns, so she uses a dire lance. Lion-O the Lion Lunar uses a sword as a badge of office. Red Fangs the Wolf lunar might not, because he is the sort who likes to go hands on. The vixen lunar though? She likes to use a bow for the opposite reason.<br /> <br /> There are numerous reasons to want to use a weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1199-mister-lion","name":"Mister Lion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T01:53:08-08:00","id":84477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84047#post84047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>My actual question was something very different, but I lost it when writing the original post and it came out all wrong.<br /> <br /> If I have any question remaining, it's something like, &quot;Why are Lunars better at Evocations than Sidereals despite a greater incentive to forego tools altogether?&quot;</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Because they're Sidereals. <i>Not</i> getting things that would be actually useful to them is kind of what Sidereals do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T07:40:29-08:00","id":84575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister Lion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84436#post84436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the animals that lack fang &amp; claw?<br /> <br /> My favorite Lunar was nicknamed 'Punchy T. Hoss'. He was a horse who... punched stuff. He used brawling aids (God-Kicking boots and Smashfists that became his horseshoes, naturally) to great effect. Sure, he could use a sword, and did from time to time, but it was not his thing.<br /> <br /> <b>Not all Lunars have predatory totems</b>, and not every lunar invests deeply into the charms allowing them to add features to their DBT form. Splish-Splash the Koi Lunar likely uses whatever weapon she can get her fins on. Lady Prances the Reindeer lunar doesn't like guts in her horns, so she uses a dire lance. Lion-O the Lion Lunar uses a sword as a badge of office. Red Fangs the Wolf lunar might not, because he is the sort who likes to go hands on. The vixen lunar though? She likes to use a bow for the opposite reason.<br /> <br /> There are numerous reasons to want to use a weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Herbivory is a form of predation, as plants are living things. Non-carnivorous totems would be a better descriptor of what you're looking for.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T08:53:47-08:00","id":84625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84575#post84575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Herbivory is a form of predation, as plants are living things. Non-carnivorous totems would be a better descriptor of what you're looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div> Was...was the pedantry necessary? I mean, though I fully get what you were saying, I know nonetheless the pedantry was inaccurate, both in terms of common usage as well as in terms of formal definition per Merriam-Webster. I'm just wondering if it was necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T09:20:21-08:00","id":84643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84575#post84575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Herbivory is a form of predation, as plants are living things. Non-carnivorous totems would be a better descriptor of what you're looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have never before in my life heard this definition of &quot;predation&quot; used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T10:05:13-08:00","id":84672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gayo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84643#post84643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have never before in my life heard this definition of &quot;predation&quot; used.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Predation#Grazing\" target=\"_blank\"> How about now?</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T10:09:41-08:00","id":84675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84672#post84672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Predation#Grazing\" target=\"_blank\"> How about now?</a></div> </div> </div> </div> Although Wikipedia is far from an ideal source, but since nonetheless the first paragraph of your Wikipedia source identifies herbivory as distinct from predation, I'm not sure what your point is. Also, as noted, check out Merriam-Webster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T10:19:48-08:00","id":84686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yishten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84675#post84675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Although Wikipedia is far from an ideal source, but since nonetheless the first paragraph of your Wikipedia source identifies herbivory as distinct from predation, I'm not sure what your point is. Also, as noted, check out Merriam-Webster.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ecology Fifth Edition by Krebs, page 206</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Herbivores are animals that prey on green plants or their seeds and fruits; often the plants eaten are not killed but may be damaged.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the effect on a living being is just like predation, why bother calling it anything else? Plants can't run, either. They can only sit around, and in the end, the least noxious ones get eaten. An arms race ensues just as if dealing with faster prey.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T10:28:07-08:00","id":84696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84686#post84686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If the effect on a living being is just like predation, why bother calling it anything else? Plants can't run, either. They can only sit around, and in the end, the least noxious ones get eaten. An arms race ensues just as if dealing with faster prey.</div> </div> </div> </div> Because words have different meanings? Like I said, I see what you're getting at. But predation has a definition in English that is distinct from the definition of herbivory and vice versa. The dictionary elucidates this. Your Wikipedia source elucidates this. Common usage and Gayo and myself all elucidate this. <br /> <br /> Cars and trucks are both four wheeled conveyances with internal combustion engines, but the terms aren't interchangeable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/926-yishten","name":"Yishten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar926_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T10:33:25-08:00","id":84699,"title":"","content":"No one cares. Calling carnivorous animals &quot;predatory&quot; and herbivorous animals something else will expand the lexicon and provide more words to use throughout a text, while also being a bit more flavorful (predatory calls different ideas to mind than just carnivorous, which sounds more clinical), and <i>no one will be confused by this, ever.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-06T05:40:45-08:00","id":85252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84477#post84477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because they're Sidereals. <i>Not</i> getting things that would be actually useful to them is kind of what Sidereals do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beyond that, it might help to compare Sidereals and Lunars a bit to understand why Lunars get what they do here; Lunars aren't very well-defined, but Sidereals and Solars are, and we can figure out a bit about Lunars from that.<br /> <br /> Sidereals are all about constraints. As a Sidereal, you have access to this hidden secret mastery, but it's all confined in a rigid framework of esoteric enlightenment which forces you to act like an eccentric mysterious old master. Evocations don't work with that because they make it too easy to break out of that theme; and unlike MA, they don't really fit the Old Master thing too closely.<br /> <br /> How many Old Masters are defined by an artifact, after all? The one I can think of is an exception that proves the rule -- <i>Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon</i>'s Mu Bai may be famous for wielding the Green Destiny, but a huge plot point is that it's not what made him a great martial artist.<br /> <br /> So what does that say about Lunars? I think that unlike Sidereals, Lunar are defined by flexibility. Lunar magic doesn't particularly need tools or swords (the way, say, Solar Melee or Solar Archery does), but Lunars are still able to take advantage of them when they have one on-hand, so they're better at evocations than Sidereals are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 03-06-2014, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T03:38:58-08:00","id":85921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84037#post84037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, <i>owning</i> a moonsilver daiklave would be attention-grabbing, such that being furry only confirms people's suspicions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd never thought of this before. Perhaps moonsilver daiklaves can be treated such that they look akin to steel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T08:52:40-08:00","id":86041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=85921#post85921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'd never thought of this before. Perhaps moonsilver daiklaves can be treated such that they look akin to steel.</div> </div> </div> </div> A daiklave is a <i>giant</i> sword. That's why simply stabbing someone with one is attention-grabbing. You either have to be inhumanly strong to swing it, or you are magical enough to attune to a magical sword which is so metallically silver it has to be moonsilver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T14:34:06-08:00","id":86272,"title":"","content":"Then whip up an evocation that turns your massive blade into a reasonably sized one when you're not in combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T15:00:36-08:00","id":86293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84686#post84686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> If the effect on a living being is just like predation, why bother calling it anything else?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>But both of the sources you've cited have said that herbivorous animals rarely kill their prey organisms, which dictionary definitions and that Wikipedia article seem to hold as the standard for being considered predation...<br /> <br /> I mean, your own linked page refers to herbivory as distinct from predation, so obviously it's saying that not all herbivores are predators.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T15:12:30-08:00","id":86301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84024#post84024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there won't have an artifact that lets them spy on their enemies for miles? You won't be able to summon a hellboar to eat corpses? Will I be able to use Evocations and Protean shapeshifting mid-combat - or will the action economy force me to take one or the other?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine the particulars could make the applications a bit different. It's useful to see things from high above, but also useful to see things from a distance that also won't leave you exposed to fire from a camp on alert for spying birds. And the difference between being or summoning something to eat a corpse seems to be largely a matter of taste.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">E2.5 gives me the choice of spending 5BPs on taking a flying horse as a Familiar, 1BP on taking an Agata as a Demonic Familiar or 8BP on learning Demon of the First Circle. They are all &quot;tools I can use to build my character&quot; but one of these options is clearly &quot;stronger&quot; than the &quot;weaker&quot; ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it though? If your only priorities are having something that can fly, the cheaper short term investment seems more worthwhile (especially if you have other things you want to spend points on). An agata might be cheaper than a horse, but it also might draw attention and also talks a lot about weird philosophy. Demon of the First Circle might have more long term utility, but you've also got to be a sorcerer and need to adhere to the terms and limits of demon summoning.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T15:20:18-08:00","id":86306,"title":"","content":"An Agata can materialize and dematerialize at will (solving the problems of appearance), teleport across large distance, is fully intelligent and has no particular puppy-killing alien urges that would make it bothersome, and is also decent in a fight. A horse that can fly is a horse that can fly.<br /> <br /> Any benefit you would derive from getting a flying horse instead of an agata (most often, none) would be off-set by its tremendous cost. There is no good design in this. There is no silver lining or thing people are blowing out of proportion. This sucks, and should be done away with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T17:14:36-08:00","id":86375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=86306#post86306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An agata can materialize and dematerialize at will</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, within the limits of its current mote pool, anyway. Which could potentially be a huge drawback, if your agata can't materialize to help you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-07T23:05:36-08:00","id":86514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84575#post84575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Herbivory is a form of predation, as plants are living things. Non-carnivorous totems would be a better descriptor of what you're looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>And how does this deal with the fact that not all Lunar concepts are sabre-toothed snow lion totems? Not every Lunar will have a suite of weapons to use in totemic form, and will use a weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1199-mister-lion","name":"Mister Lion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T06:31:54-08:00","id":86714,"title":"","content":"Also, if Lunars didn't use weapons, how would we tell them apart?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T08:09:36-08:00","id":86769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84047#post84047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are not invalid questions to ask, but you won't get the response you want from Robert because your tone is belligerent. Even when you're upset, you shouldn't phrase your questions like you want to pick a fight.<br /> [...]<br /> I don't think that's what I said? Certainly that's nothing close to what I meant to ask.<br /> [...]<br /> <b>My actual question was something very different, but I lost it when writing the original post and it came out all wrong.<br /> <br /> If I have any question remaining, it's something like, &quot;Why are Lunars better at Evocations than Sidereals despite a greater incentive to forego tools altogether?&quot;</b></div> </div> </div> </div>My apologies for misrepresenting you. That's just how I read your post. (Mostly I was biased by my interpretation of your thread title and based my previous post on &quot;why should<b>n't</b> Lunars <b>rely</b> on weapons, armour or other tools?&quot; - which I now realise is WAAAAY off-topic - sorry about the derail as well.)<br /> <br /> Also, I'm neither upset nor belligerent (at least, it's not my intent to be belligerent as I do not harangue those who do not reply directly to me). I am merely curious and desiring of clarification to inform further discourse. If I ask a question it's simply because I want more information.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84070#post84070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that this problem was pretty much directly caused by 2e being set up in such a way that a relatively high degree of specialization was required to meaningfully participate in any particular activity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bingo. It's one of the things I hope will change with 3E. Which it looks like it is.<br /> <br /> 2.5 errata took us a step in that direction (eliminating Essence-Minimum damage ping alone was huge), and 3E's starting everyone at E1, and Light/Medium/Heavy weapons seems to be continuing down that road.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84085#post84085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, wait, you don't want Solars to be forced to take an artifact weapon at chargen because you can't use your perfect parry effectively without one, but you're OK with Lunars being forced to take DBT because it has no downside whatsoever?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why does it need a downside?<br /> <br /> 1st Melee Excellency doesn't have a downside. There's no &quot;you can't use artifact weapons with this charm&quot; forcing you to choose between using your Excellency or using the artifact.<br /> <br /> (Personally, I think Lunar Knacks are an over-costed XP sink, so I tend to give my Lunar players a care package of speed-bump knacks that includes DBT - but that's neither here nor there.)<br /> <br /> I would prefer to see other Lunar Charms <i>buffed</i> (maybe even have a charm that makes Evocations stronger), so that buying DBT wasn't a no-brainer.. Incentivise other options by, you know, <b>incentivising</b> other options.<br /> <br /> Not every Lunar should be striding around in Man-Beast Form. Some of them totally should be Tony Starking it up with their awesome Evocations. The character who ignores DBT should totally be just as effective as the character that uses DBT, I just don't see why they shouldn't be allowed to Stark it up in Man-Beast Form. I'm pro-options. It's not like Solars who buy Presence Charms are forbidden from using Performance Charms: and, of course, the Solar who can use both is going to benefit from using both, just as the Solar who specialises in one is going to gain benefits from specialising. (And can you really say that the image of a shark-man calling down a tidal wave with his sword isn't a cool image - or, at least, a less clumsy image than the shark-man transforming into a shark then calling down the tidal wave with the sword clamped in its jaws?)<br /> <br /> Of course, I know no more about 3E than any of you (and a good deal less about it than some of you). So my posts could be way off the mark,<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=86301#post86301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine the particulars could make the applications a bit different [...] the difference between being or summoning something to eat a corpse seems to be largely a matter of taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>A matter of taste is a fantastic reason to have a plethora of options - build the character you want with the tools provided. The particulars of a situation are rarely a relevant concern as most STs will tailor a plot to the capabilities of the players (whether they want the players to succeed or fail). What does matter is <i>cost</i>. If I'm going to need two charms to turn into a demon pig is that going to be a good investment, a terrible investment or a game-breaking &quot;must have&quot; investment? What else could I get? What am I giving up? That is my core concern: will decisions made for RP reasons horribly cripple my character <i>mechanically</i>. Of course, it's early in the day to be asking these kinds of questions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=86301#post86301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it though? If your only priorities are having something that can fly, the cheaper short term investment seems more worthwhile (especially if you have other things you want to spend points on). An agata might be cheaper than a horse, but it also might draw attention and also talks a lot about weird philosophy. Demon of the First Circle might have more long term utility, but you've also got to be a sorcerer and need to adhere to the terms and limits of demon summoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want you to feel I'm ignoring your post: make a spin-off thread if this is something you really want to discuss, but my point was illustrative rather than definitive. Perhaps I should have compared a Grand Grimscythe to a Grand Diaklave to demonstrate that not all options are created equal.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=84047#post84047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>If I have any question remaining, it's something like, &quot;Why are Lunars better at Evocations than Sidereals despite a greater incentive to forego tools altogether?&quot;</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Aside from the established theme of Solar's being the best and DB's being the worst... is there any reason not to have parity between the (Celestial) Exalts?<br /> <br /> I mean, I know Moonsilver is not as rare as Star Metal, but should that really reflect in terms of base capability?<br /> <br /> Aquillion raises a good point about Masters rarely being defined by their tools, but I find it hard to take the comment about telling Lunar's apart by their weapons seriously (I'd assume it was a tongue in cheek comment, but my assumptions have already caused problems in this thread :P ). I mean, I don't define Leviathan by what artifacts he uses but I could totally rip off Mu Bai as a Sidreal (or B- Kiddo and her Star Metal Hanzo Sword). Wouldn't the rarity of the Sideral Evocation wielder be adequately addressed by the rarity of Star Metal? I don't see why Sid's should get the thin end of the Evocation wedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 03-08-2014, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T10:00:29-08:00","id":86828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=86769#post86769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I find it hard to take the comment about telling Lunar's apart by their weapons seriously (I'd assume it was a tongue in cheek comment, but my assumptions have already caused problems in this thread :P ). I mean, I don't define Leviathan by what artifacts he uses but I could totally rip off Mu Bai as a Sidreal (or B- Kiddo and her Star Metal Hanzo Sword). Wouldn't the rarity of the Sideral Evocation wielder be adequately addressed by the rarity of Star Metal? I don't see why Sid's should get the thin end of the Evocation wedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think It's a reference to how 1e Exalted: The Lunars actually had a sidebar telling you that the way to tell Lunars apart is by maybe trying to pick different weapons for them.<br /> <br /> Also, I do recall the devs talking about how DBT is going to be treated as &quot;that tool you relied on when you were young and inexperienced&quot; more than a must-have for any and all Lunars (with it hopefully being very upgradeable for those that <i>do</i> want to keep using that tool).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T13:20:36-08:00","id":86963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=86828#post86828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I do recall the devs talking about how DBT is going to be treated as &quot;that tool you relied on when you were young and inexperienced&quot; more than a must-have for any and all Lunars (with it hopefully being very upgradeable for those that <i>do</i> want to keep using that tool).</div> </div> </div> </div>From the quote itself, that feels like the intent to me:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't want to be a DBT Lunar, I'd rather you think of DBT / spirit shape as the tool you relied on when your Lunar was still young, inexperienced, and less powerful, rather than ignoring it entirely. I want to help people build away from a DBT-based character through powers that work when you are in your human form and don't work when you are in DBT.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think of DBT as an extension on the philosophy suggested by more typical shapeshifting. By which I mean, a Lunar has a plethora of shapes at his disposal, but no shape is better in <i>all</i> situations. A Lunar's likely going to pick something like a sparrow when he wants something that can fly discretely, and something bigger and more dangerous when he wants something that can fly and fight. Even in the realm of &quot;creatures that can fight,&quot; there's variety in the options each has available.* In various situations, all have their individual upsides and downsides. A Lunar looks at the situation and picks a shape that's going to get plenty of the one and relatively few of the other. Picking the right shape for a situation feels like a sizeable piece of playing a Lunar, so there's value in designing things such that no particular shape feels overwhelmingly powerful. From there comes the idea of giving DBT the minus that a Lunar can't utilize Evocations (which are potent) when it's active, and the plus that it's designed such that a Lunar <i>can still </i>find it to be a legitimately good option to consider <i>even if</i> they've spent time and effort learning Evocations.<br /> <br /> * By the sound of it, EX3's combat system and animal stats alone will be varied and context-sensitive enough to actually reflect this, so woo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=86769#post86769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't the rarity of the Sideral Evocation wielder be adequately addressed by the rarity of Star Metal? I don't see why Sid's should get the thin end of the Evocation wedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the issue here is that you're looking at things in a straight Evocation-to-Evocation comparison in a vacuum. That would only be valid if Lunars and Sids had equal capabilities outside Evocations, but Lunars just happened to be better with them. So two points I'd make for how Sids not doing so hot with Evocations can work out:<br /> <br /> 1) A general statement is all we've got. We don't have reason to think this is going to be like 2e's &quot;These power levels are only for Solars, these are only for Celestials, these are only for Terrestrials, and ne'er shall a being from a lower tier see power from a higher,&quot; nor do we have reason to think there are, say, Solar Circle Evocations, with further Circles extending on down, with Siddies getting the shaft. Basically, we don't know this is a hard delineation. There could be some Artifacts where Solars and Lunars have equal access to its Evocations, Artifacts where Sidereals and Lunars have equal Evocation access (with Solars above them), some Artifacts where Sidereals have better Evocation access than Lunars, etc. In fact, since we've heard talk about how &quot;Dragon-Blooded have a special dispensation which will be explained in future books&quot; regarding Evocations, that suggests it may not be so clear-cut.<br /> <br /> 2) Characters get access to particular Evocations as an option in the context of all their other splat-specific options and capabilities. Let's take a hypothetical Starmetal daiklave. Let's say Solars can use all the weapon's Evocations, while a Sidereal can only use some or most of them. In a direct comparison like that, of course the Solar comes out on top. But that would be silly, because Sidereals have a ton of capabilities that are hard or impossible for the vast majority of other non-Sidereals to pull off. We know the devs are keeping an eye on synergies -- John said mid-tree Solar Charms aren't meant to look so impressive on their own, but <i>are</i> meant to really buff or expand options a Solar purchased earlier in the tree. So perhaps the Evocations in the Starmetal daiklave that a Sidereal <i>can</i> use are ones that become especially dangerous or impressive when viewed in the context of native Sidereal Charms, Sidereal Martial Arts, or Sidereal Astrology. On that last note, it's even conceivable there may be Evocations that spell out such synergies: maybe that daiklave's Evocations are handy enough for a Solar, but clearly have special effects written in for a user with access to Sidereal Astrology, elevating it to being straight-up <i>amazing</i>. These kinds of things can make it an open question whether a Solar or Sidereal is more powerful with a given Artifact. Or even where, in terms of raw combat potency, the Solar's definitely on top, but raw combat potency isn't really the benefit the Sidereal is trying to derive from it: in the end, it might feel like an apples-to-oranges comparison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 03-08-2014, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T16:11:09-08:00","id":87062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=86769#post86769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why does it need a downside?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because some people don't want to use DBT, and they don't want to feel stupid for doing so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1st Melee Excellency doesn't have a downside. There's no &quot;you can't use artifact weapons with this charm&quot; forcing you to choose between using your Excellency or using the artifact. </div> </div> </div>1st Melee Excellency doesn't force you to have certain aesthetics. If 1st Melee Excellency was the only Excellency that existed, people would complain because Melee would be better than other fighting Abilities, and this would suck for people who want to use a bow. Similarly, people complain because DBT is better than no-DBT.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The character who ignores DBT should totally be just as effective as the character that uses DBT </div> </div> </div>That is impossible because, no matter your fighting style, no matter what other Charms you use, having DBT is always superior to not having DBT. Which means that, if you don't use DBT because you don't want to look like a man-beast while you fight, you are in fact making a mechanically stupid decision.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would prefer to see other Lunar Charms <i>buffed</i> (maybe even have a charm that makes Evocations stronger), so that buying DBT wasn't a no-brainer.. Incentivise other options by, you know, <b>incentivising</b> other options. </div> </div> </div>No matter how strong Lunar Charms are, someone who has both strong Lunar Charms and DBT is still better than someone who only has strong Lunar Charms.<br /> <br /> You really can't make DBT anything other but a must-have without putting in downsides.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is my core concern: will decisions made for RP reasons horribly cripple my character <i>mechanically</i>. </div> </div> </div>You take the words right out of my mouth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","user":"Kazorh","date":". 03-08-2014, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T16:27:48-08:00","id":87070,"title":"","content":"As for Evocations: my impression when the devs talk about Solars being the best with Evocations is that they can use the Evocations of any and all artifacts, no matter what they're made of. I don't actually remember if this is from an actual quote or just a figment of my imagination (and I'm too lazy to check the What We Know). From this, one could assume that Sidereals not being so good with Evocations doesn't mean that they can't learn strong Evocations, but rather that they're limited to using the Evocations of starmetal artifacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","user":"Kazorh","date":". 03-08-2014, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-08T22:44:38-08:00","id":87252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=87062#post87062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That is impossible because, no matter your fighting style, no matter what other Charms you use, having DBT is always superior to not having DBT. Which means that, if you don't use DBT because you don't want to look like a man-beast while you fight, you are in fact making a mechanically stupid decision.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No matter how strong Lunar Charms are, someone who has both strong Lunar Charms and DBT is still better than someone who only has strong Lunar Charms.<br /> <br /> You really can't make DBT anything other but a must-have without putting in downsides.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You're very certain of this, but its entirely possible that this isn't true. DBT is a tool in the toolbox of a Lunar. DBT will allow for certain things, but not DBT charms will do things DBT cannot do. It's a matter of playstyle, not a choice of what is the superior option.<br /> <br /> I feel we've been spoiled on games looking for the superior options, and this won't have any, just many different options, not one stronger or weaker than another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T05:26:02-07:00","id":87435,"title":"","content":"The more i see this thread crop up on the front page, the more it confuses me.<br /> It's like all the &quot;Anti-Lunars-Having-Weapons&quot; faction have never run a non-DBT Lunar in 2e.<br /> <br /> I mean, no matter how you look at it you can justify lunars using tools:<br /> -Thematically, Lunars are not &quot;The DBT splat&quot; they're the &quot;Shapechanging splat&quot;. My current Lunar does not have DBT because thematically he is a trickster and gambler. Hulking war beast does not suit every Lunar.<br /> <br /> -Stuff like Butterfly Eyes Defence and Weapon Shaping Method work BETTER without relying on DBT. Because it falls into &quot;Lunars are tricksters&quot; purview of their charms. And it's difficult to play mindgames as a half Wolf-half Man with mutated Tentacles. Unless that mindgame is &quot;Pants-shitting-terror&quot;<br /> <br /> -I am in an all Lunars game. Every one of us relying on DBT would be boring as hell and i wanted to explore other viable options. Infact only 2 of us went DBT. I would like more reasons to do this in the new edition not less.<br /> <br /> In my mind that's tool using Lunars justified from a fluff, mechanics and fun point of view. There is a large spectrum of Lunar concepts that either don't want or need DBT to be doing Lunar theme-d stuff.<br /> Being the only splat that can pretend to be a street performing monkey, or slip unoticed into a noble's aquariam, or soar through the skies unnoticed should be enough reason to want to use them, with becoming HULKING DEATH BEAST as an option not a pre-requisite. They are versatile, let them be versatile.<br /> <br /> I mean, don't get me wrong, i love me some HULKING DEATH BEAST. But i don't like the idea every Lunar needs it. Or it can't exist with any other form of Lunar. It's not, nor it should be their only gimmick<br /> <br /> I mean, sure if i wanted to make THE MOST COMBAT VIABLE LUNAR maybe i'm not doing it right. But i'm not a combat Lunar, i'm a lunar who values subtlety and manipulation. And that's Lunar too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1397-parallel","name":"Parallel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T06:16:49-07:00","id":87451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godjaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=87252#post87252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're very certain of this, but its entirely possible that this isn't true. DBT is a tool in the toolbox of a Lunar. DBT will allow for certain things, but not DBT charms will do things DBT cannot do. It's a matter of playstyle, not a choice of what is the superior option.<br /> <br /> I feel we've been spoiled on games looking for the superior options, and this won't have any, just many different options, not one stronger or weaker than another.</div> </div> </div> </div>You realize I'm talking about the 2e version, right? &quot;Boosts all physical Attributes, lets you use Gift Charms, lets you have mutations of your own choosing, stacks with everything, has no downside whatsoever&quot;? Yes, I'm &quot;very certain&quot; that, from the point of view of mechanics, this is in fact something that everyone should pick.<br /> <br /> I am <i>all about</i> DBT and no-DBT being &quot;different options, not one stronger or weaker than another&quot;. <i>That's why I support the idea of making Evocations unavailable in DBT.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","user":"Kazorh","date":". 03-09-2014, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T06:38:43-07:00","id":87454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Parallel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=87435#post87435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My current Lunar does not have DBT because thematically he is a trickster and gambler. Hulking war beast does not suit every Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here we see the non-DBT-user in his natural habitat: Internet forums. Don't worry, non-DBT-user, I'm crusading for your rights. (By having a random argument with people who have no power to change Ex3. :P )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","user":"Kazorh","date":". 03-09-2014, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T07:32:00-07:00","id":87469,"title":"","content":"I think when we're all talking on the internet, it's kind of petty to mock some opinions by saying they're held by people on the internet. I mean, we're all arguing with people who have no ability to change ex3. This is an internet forum. Which you, sir, are posting on.<br /> <br /> I think every Lunar I've seen played has had DBT... it's just too good not to have, essentially. But they've not necessarily wanted to have it, they haven't felt it was thematic. One guy took the (terrible) small mutation for his bunny-Lunar's DBT, because he thought hulking beast monster didn't fit the character (and I think he was right).<br /> Most characters it does work fine for (I mean, you are playing a shapeshifter already), but not all.<br /> <br /> Another thing I hope is dropped about DBT is the way some totems make much better DBTs than others. If your totem is snake, you have access to much better mutations than if your totem is, say, a dog. Or a monkey. Monkeys are pretty terrible DBT-wise.<br /> But I imagine this will get fixed because of changes to the mutation system.<br /> <br /> I don't know if I like this idea of DBT meaning no evocations... it seems kind of simplistic, but that doesn't make it bad. And I guess using magical weapons vs turning into a giant monster and shredding people do work as sensible alternative structures. Essentially, I have very little idea of what sort of things evocations are going to do. I'd really like them to spoil an evocation charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T07:33:26-07:00","id":87470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=87454#post87454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Here we see the non-DBT-user in his natural habitat: Internet forums. Don't worry, non-DBT-user, I'm crusading for your rights. (By having a random argument with people who have no power to change Ex3. :P )</div> </div> </div> </div>By the fact you have over 200 more posts than me, shouldn't it be the reverse? :P<br /> <br /> Besides, i think the Devs are the one's crusading for non-DBT Lunar rights. By writing them in a way which sounds like they won't default to DBT because they'll be written in a way that doesn't assume they'll have DBT.<br /> (Which, to be fair, 2e does, but weapon Lunars in 2e &quot;have a bunch of cool tricks&quot; wheras DBT has &quot;All the power and MOST of the cool tricks weapon Lunars have&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1397-parallel","name":"Parallel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T07:39:44-07:00","id":87474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Parallel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=87470#post87470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;All the power and MOST of the cool tricks weapon Lunars have&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>Besides the xp cost, are there any cool tricks DBT doesn't let you use?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T08:21:02-07:00","id":87498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=87451#post87451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You realize I'm talking about the second edition version [of Deadly Beastman Transformation], right?</div> </div> </div> </div>But then you say:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=87451#post87451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why I support the idea of making Evocations unavailable in Deadly Beastman Transformation.</div> </div> </div> </div>It just...it really sounds like you're arguing about what third edition should be based not on what third edition is, but what second edition was. It's like saying third edition Infernals should have Charms that to sever their Exaltations from Lillun, even though Lillun won't exist in third edition.<br /> <br /> Let's wait to see what Deadly Beastman Transformation even is before we start arguing about whether you should be allowed to use Evocations while Hyde-ing out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T09:21:18-07:00","id":87530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=87474#post87474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides the xp cost, are there any cool tricks DBT doesn't let you use?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Blade Reconfiguration requires having a moonsilver weapon.(And a similar situation for its pre-requisites)<br /> Mystic Butterfly Fraud loses all its in-battle applications without having some sort of weapon.<br /> They're the only 2 I could spot flicking through the Lunar core, but i may have missed one or two.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's not many, there's certainly more combat charms enhanced by DBT than those rendered invalid, but they're THERE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1397-parallel","name":"Parallel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T12:38:08-07:00","id":87666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=87469#post87469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially, I have very little idea of what sort of things evocations are going to do. I'd really like them to spoil an evocation charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure you know this already, but if you're feeling shaky on Evocations, you can browse through the <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Exalted_3E:_What_We_Know#Evocations\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations section</a> of the What We Know Wiki to see if it helps. We do have this, though:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sample of Evocations: The daiklave called Stormcaller sleeps in its sheathe. When drawn, a hurricane begins to form overhead. Its Evocations both draw from the storm's ferocity, and add to it. The character must carefully draw down and disperse the storm before sheathing Stormcaller. Apex Evocation involves sheathing the weapon early to disperse the storm in a massive directional stormblast capable of flooring a behemoth.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Parallel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=87530#post87530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar Blade Reconfiguration requires having a moonsilver weapon.(And a similar situation for its pre-requisites)<br /> Mystic Butterfly Fraud loses all its in-battle applications without having some sort of weapon.<br /> They're the only 2 I could spot flicking through the Lunar core, but i may have missed one or two.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's not many, there's certainly more combat charms enhanced by DBT than those rendered invalid, but they're THERE.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhh... Am I missing something enormous here? How does DBT render any of those invalid? A Lunar in DBT can still use artifact weapons, last I recalled, and so... would be fine with them? If not, then... How the hell has that not been a bigger complaint on Lunars before? o_o","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T16:04:05-07:00","id":87786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=87469#post87469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think when we're all talking on the internet, it's kind of petty to mock some opinions by saying they're held by people on the internet. I mean, we're all arguing with people who have no ability to change ex3. This is an internet forum. Which you, sir, are posting on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err, are you talking to me? I'm sorry if it offended you; I didn't mean to mock anyone. If anything, it was supposed to be self-deprecating: &quot;I am a valiant crusader defending people! Actually not really.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=87498#post87498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just...it really sounds like you're arguing about what third edition should be based not on what third edition is, but what second edition was. It's like saying third edition Infernals should have Charms that to sever their Exaltations from Lillun, even though Lillun won't exist in third edition.<br /> <br /> Let's wait to see what Deadly Beastman Transformation even is before we start arguing about whether you should be allowed to use Evocations while Hyde-ing out.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is: if they don't want DBT to be considered a must-have in Ex3, then there must actually be reasons why you would not want to use DBT. This is true for any given power in any given game. My point would remain even if 2e DBT did not exist.<br /> <br /> Not being able to use Evocations seems reasonable. You have good reasons to fight in human shape, and you still have good reasons to fight using DBT. But it's not the Evocation-lock specifically that I like, it's the idea that they've decided to put some kind of downside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T16:09:48-07:00","id":87789,"title":"","content":"DBT is actually quite compatible with weapons in 2E/2.5E, and this is a big part of why it was a no-brainer whenever combat broke out. That said, I could definitely see 3E's DBT being less of a binary &quot;Natural Weapons vs. Manufactured Weapons&quot; since that'd just pigeonhole characters along different lines. In human form, you have access to Evocations and certain Techniques and the like; in War Form, you lose those but gain all the benefits you'd expect of claws like meat-cleavers or a sword the size of a surfboard backed by enough strength to chop an armored man in two like a head of cabbage. More of a stance system where you shift moment-to-moment depending on your immediate needs than a painfully-straitjackety charbuild dichotomy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T21:59:07-07:00","id":87944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=87786#post87786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Err, are you talking to me? I'm sorry if it offended you; I didn't mean to mock anyone. If anything, it was supposed to be self-deprecating: &quot;I am a valiant crusader defending people! Actually not really.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I hate not being able to read people's body language and hear their tone on the internet. I apologise.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T22:13:35-07:00","id":87964,"title":"","content":"Haha, yeah. And no harm done. It's kind of amusing actually: one reason I decided to include the joke in my post is that I've been told I can sound a bit harsh when I go into argumentative mode. So this was totally meant to make me look softer so people wouldn't think I was going to bite their heads off for disagreeing with me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T22:23:56-07:00","id":87970,"title":"","content":"The same thing happened to me in the DB exaltation thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure you know this already, but if you're feeling shaky on Evocations, you can browse through the <a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/ExaltedWiki/mediawiki-1.19.1/index.php?title=Exalted_3E:_What_We_Know#Evocations\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations section</a> of the What We Know Wiki to see if it helps. We do have this, though:</div> </div> </div> </div>I did, but actually there's more on there than the last time I read it, so thanks.<br /> <br /> Anyway, essentially I don't know how desirable being able to use evocations in combat will be for Lunars. Presumably the devs consider it good enough that it's worth making that the downside to DBT.<br /> <br /> I also wonder if they're going to literally write evocations for every single weapon, or do something like: here's a bunch of evocations, pick 2 when you buy a weapon at character creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T22:28:37-07:00","id":87973,"title":"","content":"I got the feeling that not every weapon would come with an evocation. Sometimes your giant surfboard of a sword and your heroic strength is enough.<br /> <br /> Also, I think evocations allow you to 'level up' the weapon with you. If your beginning Solar liberates her First Age version's dire-spear from the Dream of the Five Cornered Tomb, you can have the weapon grow and become more powerful as you do. You're unlocking its full potential or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T22:32:28-07:00","id":87975,"title":"","content":"That's the impression I got, and it would be a good idea. I just wonder how it will work in practice.<br /> <br /> Also, if the evocations are weapon-specific, then presumably they're not going to bother writing seperate evocations for each different Exalt type to use with the weapon. So I'd assume they'll write something like: Charm does X, but gets extra benefit Y if you're a Solar. Or maybe there are 5 charms that can be bought, but only Solars can buy the top one.<br /> Or most of the time only Solars can buy them, but some say &quot;DBs can also buy this&quot; or &quot;Lunars can also buy this&quot;, or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T20:58:03-07:00","id":91367,"title":"","content":"I forgot that this thread exists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=87786#post87786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is, if they don't want Deadly Beastman Transformation to be considered a must-have in third edition, then there must actually be reasons why you would not want to use Deadly Beastman Transformation. This is true for any given power in any given game. My point would remain even if second edition Deadly Beastman Transformation did not exist.<br /> <br /> Not being able to use Evocations seems reasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div>But your premise relies upon the assumption that it's going to be close enough to second edition's version that it needs nerfing right out of the box rather than being internally balanced by factors like synergy with its own Charm tech, cost, and effectiveness. I reserve judgment until I see implementation of the thing, but I have a very hard time imagining I can support any power in any splat's Charm tech that actually denies you access to other abilities and effects you paid for with your own character points. The only example I can think of when they tried that in second edition is that one Ebby Charm that denies you access to Virtue channels, and that only worked because it gave you a bunch of benefits in exchange for something no one ever used anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T23:34:50-07:00","id":91434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=91367#post91367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But your premise relies upon the assumption that it's going to be close enough to second edition's version that it needs nerfing right out of the box rather than being internally balanced by factors like synergy with its own Charm tech, cost, and effectiveness.</div> </div> </div> </div>See also: &quot;then there must actually be reasons why you would not want to use Deadly Beastman Transformation&quot;. If it sucks, or it costs enough to use that it would be a noticeable drain on your Essence pool (even with the 5 motes per turn in-combat regen) (do we know if Essence commitment is still a thing?), then those are reasons not to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T06:53:20-07:00","id":94237,"title":"","content":"Look at Mystique from the X-Men. She is pure lunar, and she uses weapons often - mostly guns. As far as I remember, Envy from Fullmetal Alchemist used a gun on a specific beloved character.<br /> There are lots of shapeshifters in fiction who use all sorts of weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1372-locke","name":"Locke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T15:51:55-07:00","id":94515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Locke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=94237#post94237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at Mystique from the X-Men. She is pure lunar</div> </div> </div> </div>The developers explicit deny that Mystique is a good direct inspiration for Lunar Exalted. A Lunar can do what she does, but she's not really a Lunar.<br /> <br /> In the same breath, they also say that T-1000 isn't appropriate Lunar inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T07:44:18-07:00","id":97516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=87469#post87469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing I hope is dropped about DBT is the way some totems make much better DBTs than others. If your totem is snake, you have access to much better mutations than if your totem is, say, a dog. Or a monkey. Monkeys are pretty terrible DBT-wise.<br /> But I imagine this will get fixed because of changes to the mutation system.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, but it becomes irrelevant with Perfected Hybrid Interaction, which you can take as a starting character, and moreso with HBR if you have the motes to spend. I much prefer being a shapeless avatar of destruction to an anthro version of a particular animal anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=87469#post87469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if I like this idea of DBT meaning no evocations... it seems kind of simplistic, but that doesn't make it bad. And I guess using magical weapons vs turning into a giant monster and shredding people do work as sensible alternative structures. Essentially, I have very little idea of what sort of things evocations are going to do. I'd really like them to spoil an evocation charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. It sounds very arbitrary to me. Why would having fur and/or claws prevent you from using evocations? If that's the case, then what about ordinary beastmen who become Exalted? Can they not use evocations at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2536,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","user":"TSk","date":". 03-24-2014, 10:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T07:54:43-07:00","id":97519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TSk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/79003-why-should-lunars-use-weapons-armor-or-other-tools?p=97516#post97516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's true, but it becomes irrelevant with Perfected Hybrid Interaction, which you can take as a starting character, and moreso with HBR if you have the motes to spend. I much prefer being a shapeless avatar of destruction to an anthro version of a particular animal anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's certainly true, mechanically, but a lot of players are going to want to turn into a giant anthro version of their spirit shape. I use HBR, (so my owl totem No Moon turns into a stone, clawed, monster, I need the soak more than the wings as I can grow them with HBR anyway) because that character is an unstable mutant anyway, I think it fits. But other characters fit better as, say, a giant weretiger man because they're totem is a tiger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T08:25:44-07:00","id":97536,"title":"","content":"Some players will want that, yeah. I just meant that you can make your monkey DBT as deadly as the tiger totem's DBT with Perfected Hybrid Interaction.<br /> <br /> To answer the OP's question, the best reason I can think of for using a daiklave or other weapon is because you have an ST who lets you stunt Many-Pockets Meditation to summon it out of your own arm (&quot;elsewhere&quot;) when needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2536-tsk","name":"TSk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2536_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}